IVSR now recognizes the affine form (iv + k) * stride in addition to the plain
iv * stride: the pointer induction variable is initialized to
base + (init + k) * stride instead of base + init * stride. Non-constant IV
inits with a non-zero affine offset fall back conservatively to scalar code.

